# =============================================================================
# experiment/contactangle/relax_T-20_theta30.opts
#
# Isothermal, sealed relaxation of a confined ice grain, for the contact-angle
# validation. The SURFACE ENERGIES are the input here; theta is derived by the
# solver from Young's equation and printed in the banner. That is the point of
# the test -- the solver is handed gamma's, not an angle.
#
#     cos(theta) = (gamma_as - gamma_is)/gamma_ia
#                = (0.300000 - 0.205603)/0.109000
#                = +0.866025     ->  theta = 30.000 deg
#
# gamma_ia = 0.109 J/m^2 is Sigma_i, the ice-vapour surface energy this solver
# already implies: inverting monitoring.c's d0 = Etai*V_m/(R*T) at the physical
# d0_sub0 = 1.0166e-9 m and -20 C returns exactly that. gamma_as = 0.3 J/m^2
# is a plausible regolith-vapour value; only the DIFFERENCE gamma_as - gamma_is
# enters the wall term, so the pair is what matters, not either alone.
#
# Phase change is ON. -decouple_phase_change would give faster, cleaner
# curvature relaxation, but with the sublimation source zeroed the ice has no
# transport mechanism at all and the model is no longer the thing being
# validated. Relaxation here is vapour-diffusion limited.
#
# Sealed box (-flag_BC_rhovfix 0, the solver default): total water is conserved
# between ice and vapour, so the bridge settles to an equilibrium shape instead
# of evaporating away. Do NOT pin vapour on the wall faces -- lunar_main.c
# warns that doing so feeds ice at the contact line and corrupts the angle.
#
# -dtmax is deliberately NOT set here. It has to scale with eps (tau_sub goes
# as eps^2), and this file is shared across three resolutions, so it lives in
# the geometry file instead. Setting it here would override the geometry's
# value -- options files are applied geometry-then-experiment -- which is the
# bug that stalled the eps = 0.75 um run of batch 2026-09-12.
#
# t_final = 65 days, sized from the pilot run rather than guessed:
#   studies/contact_angle/verification/ records tau = 14.4 days for the approach
#   theta(t) = theta_inf + A*exp(-t/tau) on the eps3.00um channel. 65 days is
#   4.5*tau, which lands within ~1 deg of equilibrium. Relaxation is
#   vapour-diffusion limited and genuinely this slow; the first ~2 days run the
#   other way while the grain shrinks under Gibbs-Thomson until the sealed box's
#   vapour saturates.
#
# Even so, contact_angle.py reports theta_inf from a free three-parameter fit,
# so the equilibrium angle is recovered even if a run stops short -- the
# relaxation is a very clean single exponential (fit RMS 0.015 deg). Read
# theta_inf, and check theta(t) in plots/contact_angle.png either way.
# =============================================================================
-t_final 5.616e6

-temp -20.0
-humidity 1.00
-grad_temp0 0.0,0.0,0.0

-beta_sub0 3.9704e6                     # K&P beta0 at -20 C (alpha_c = 2e-3)
-d0_sub0 1.0166e-9                      # physical capillary length at -20 C

# --- the substrate, as surface energies ---
-gamma_ia 0.109
-gamma_as 0.3
-gamma_is 0.2056032

-dtCFL 1
-dtCFL_dphimax 0.2
-outp 0
-n_out 60
